  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Blocks placed inside rich text now keep their reference through translation. A block dropped into the middle of a rich-text field is stored as a reference; the export used to send the field's display form, which drops that reference, so the translated page showed the block's name as plain text instead of rendering the block. The export now sends the stored form, the reference travels with the file, and the block renders on the translated page. Links and images in rich text are exported as permanent links rather than resolved URLs, so they keep working when their target is moved or renamed. Plain rich-text content is unchanged, and files from projects submitted before this release still import as before. Pages translated before this release carry the broken reference in their translated versions and need re-exporting and re-delivering to repair. A block's own translatable Name property defined in code (a chart series label, for example) now receives its translation; it used to be written to the block's built-in name, leaving the required property empty so publish failed with \"Property 'Name' is required\". The block's built-in name stays in the source language, page-name translation works as before, and projects submitted before this release still import correctly.",
